</tbody>
</table>

<p>The chart above shows the dramatic upward structural break in 1973–74 (the Arab Oil Embargo), followed by the second shock in 1979–80 (Iranian Revolution / Iran-Iraq War). Prices then entered a prolonged bear market from the mid-1980s through the late 1990s. The 2000s brought the commodity super-cycle, peaking in mid-2008 at ${fmt(max_price)}/bbl before the Global Financial Crisis halved prices in months. A rapid recovery into 2011–2014 gave way to the shale-driven correction of 2014–2016. The COVID-19 pandemic produced an extraordinary demand shock in early 2020, followed by a strong rebound through 2022 when prices again breached $110/bbl.</p>

